Third-party notices for text recognition
=========================================

Gamma recognizes the text of scanned PDF pages with Tesseract, through the
tesserocr Python package (backend/gamma/ocr_engine.py). The tesserocr wheels
bundle the Tesseract library, Leptonica and the image libraries below inside
the server's Python environment: the Docker image and the desktop app ship
them as built. The models in this folder are Tesseract's (README.md). Where
the server has no engine of its own, the window that asks reads the pages
with tesseract.js, which the web app's build ships (the last section). Each
component keeps its own licence; their notices follow.

Which libraries a wheel bundles depends on its platform. The Linux wheels
(manylinux_2_28, x86_64 and aarch64) carry libtesseract, Leptonica, libtiff,
libpng, libjpeg, libwebp and JBIG-KIT, and the macOS wheels the like; the
Windows wheel carries giflib, OpenJPEG and zlib as well, and more besides
(ICU, OpenSSL, libcurl, libssh2, libarchive, zstd, xz, bzip2, lz4,
libdeflate, LERC, libxml2, libiconv, krb5, libpsl and the Microsoft C++
runtime); their licence texts travel in that wheel's own metadata
(tesserocr-2.13.0.dist-info/licenses), which the desktop app's frozen
backend copies beside the package.

